 own flesh and blood. So why should you be the last to restore the king?’","from":14},{"book":"2SA","chapter":19,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"And say to Amasa, ‘Arenʼt you my flesh and blood? May God punish me, and ever so severely, if from now on you are not the commander of my army in place of Joab!’”","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The girl ran and told her motherʼs household about these things.","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And when some shepherds came along and drove them away, Moses rose up to help them and watered their flock.","from":10},{"book":"JDG","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Whenever the Israelites planted their crops, the Midianites, Amalekites, and other people of the east would come up and invade them,","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And the man said: “This is now bone of my bones and flesh of my flesh; she shall be called ‘woman,’ for out of man she was taken.”","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So Abram said to Lot, “Please let there be no contention between you and me, or between your herdsmen and my herdsmen. After all, we are kinsmen.","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]},"15-30":{"people":[{"id":"laban-h3837a","name":"Laban","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bethuel","count":9,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"rachel-h7354","name":"Rachel","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Leah","count":8,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"leah-h3812","name":"Leah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Rachel","count":6,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"zilpah-h2153","name":"Zilpah","kind":"person","brief