from":30},{"book":"EXO","chapter":22,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"If a man seduces a virgin who is not pledged in marriage and sleeps with her, he must pay the full dowry for her to be his wife.","from":18},{"book":"EXO","chapter":22,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"If her father absolutely refuses to give her to him, the man still must pay an amount comparable to the bridal price of a virgin.","from":18},{"book":"JDG","chapter":15,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Later on, at the time of the wheat harvest, Samson took a young goat and went to visit his wife. “I want to go to my wife in her room,” he said. But her father would not let him enter.","from":21},{"book":"HOS","chapter":12,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Jacob fled to the land of Aram and Israel worked for a wife— for a wife he tended sheep.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":6}]},"31-35":{"people":[{"id":"leah-h3812","name":"Leah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Rachel","count":2,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"rachel-h7354","name":"Rachel","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Leah","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"simeon-h8095g","name":"Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":35}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2029","lemma":"הָרָה","tr":"ha·rah","gloss":"to conceive","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":43},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":496},{"base":"H7121","lemma":"קָרָא","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to call: call to","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"us